Host work per GPU op, with the same commands and the same bytes on the GPU.

A command buffer takes one completion handler for every buffer its ops read,
in place of one handler per evaluated array. A custom kernel instantiation
(template arguments, how each input is passed, the dtypes) writes its name, its
source and its library name once and every later call shares them, in place of
writing the source and hashing all of it on each call. Metal only.

